            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that a sole owner may be a participant in an employee benefit plan if another common law employee participates, regardless of whether the entity operates as a sole proprietorship, partnership, or corporation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "fff05b50381f390659d296ee44f16dd963268263b691bd4d2f78e445713e39d9",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-fff05b50381f-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States, as amicus, contends that all working owners\u2014including shareholders, partners, and sole proprietors\u2014should be treated as participants under ERISA, just like other employees."
      }
    ],
